workedExamples.question_text:
Sketch the front, back, right-side and top views of this trapezoidal prism. The front is the nearer trapezium-shaped end. Draw the top view with the prism's length running down the page.

[tikz]
% mathsmap-solid {"version":1,"kind":"polyhedron","model":{"version":1,"kind":"polyhedron","vertices":{"A":[0,0,0],"B":[3,0,0],"C":[2.25,2,0],"D":[0.75,2,0],"E":[0,0,3],"F":[3,0,3],"G":[2.25,2,3],"H":[0.75,2,3]},"faces":[["A","D","C","B"],["E","F","G","H"],["A","B","F","E"],["B","C","G","F"],["C","D","H","G"],["D","A","E","H"]],"view":{"right":[1,0,0.5],"up":[0,1,0.35],"toward":[0.5,0.35,-1]}}}
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (3,0); \coordinate (C) at (2.25,2); \coordinate (D) at (0.75,2);
\coordinate (E) at (1.5,1.05); \coordinate (F) at (4.5,1.05); \coordinate (G) at (3.75,3.05); \coordinate (H) at (2.25,3.05);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw (B)--(F)--(G)--(H)--(D);
\draw (C)--(G);
\draw[dashed] (A)--(E)--(F); \draw[dashed] (E)--(H);
\draw[->] (1.5,-1)--(1.5,-0.2); \path (1.5,-1) node[below]{Front};
\draw[->] (5.4,1.5)--(4.6,1.5); \path (5.4,1.5) node[right]{Right side};
\draw[->] (2.8,4.1)--(2.8,3.3); \path (2.8,4.1) node[above]{Top};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
The front view shows the trapezium-shaped end. The back view is its mirror image; this end face has left-right symmetry, so both views look identical.

The right-side outline is a rectangle. Looking horizontally, the sloping side projects to the prism's full height.

The top outline is a rectangle. Include the two edges where the flat top meets the sloping faces.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\begin{scope}
\draw (0,0)--(3,0)--(2.25,2)--(0.75,2)--cycle;
\path (1.5,-0.5) node{Front};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(4.3,0)}]
\draw (0,0)--(3,0)--(2.25,2)--(0.75,2)--cycle;
\path (1.5,-0.5) node{Back};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(0,-4.5)}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3,2);
\path (1.5,-0.5) node{Right side};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(4.3,-4.5)}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
\draw (0.75,0)--(0.75,3); \draw (2.25,0)--(2.25,3);
\path (1.5,-0.5) node{Top};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

